  "prefLabel": "Env-A 1802.34 Maintenance worker",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-A 1802.34 “Maintenance worker” means an individual who engages in work activities designed or intended to contribute to the on-going routine maintenance of a facility, including but not limited to building maintenance, electrical work, plumbing, carpentry, masonry, custodial services, and heating services, and whose primary occupation is not asbestos abatement.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note #1, Revision Note #2, and Revision Note #3 at chapter heading for Env-A 1800) #14104, eff 11-1-24, EXPIRES: 11-1-34",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-a1800.html"
